WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.942
Wendy, John, and Michael sailed home.

2
00:00:03.943 --> 00:00:11.503
As they enjoyed the salty ocean breeze and the rolling waves, they imagined their homecoming at Number 14.

3
00:00:11.504 --> 00:00:19.735
They pictured their mother’s delight, their father’s shout of joy, and Nana’s leap to embrace them.

4
00:00:19.736 --> 00:00:24.738
In fact, everything in the nursery was already prepared for them.

5
00:00:24.739 --> 00:00:34.592
The beds were made, the window was open, and Mrs. Darling was waiting—just as she had every day since they had left.

6
00:00:34.593 --> 00:00:42.939
The only change was that between nine in the morning and six at night Nana’s dog house was not in the nursery.

7
00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:47.734
When the children flew away, Mr. Darling felt that he was to blame.

8
00:00:47.735 --> 00:00:52.538
After all, he had chained up Nana and left the children alone.

9
00:00:52.539 --> 00:00:57.037
Nana, he realized, had been the wise one.

10
00:00:57.038 --> 00:01:02.903
If anyone deserved to be locked up, Mr. Darling decided, it was he.

11
00:01:02.904 --> 00:01:06.852
He crawled into Nana’s dog house and wouldn’t allow her in.

12
00:01:06.853 --> 00:01:13.801
When Mrs. Darling begged him to come out, he said, "No, dear, this is where I belong."

13
00:01:13.802 --> 00:01:20.288
He swore that he would never leave the dog house until his children came back.

14
00:01:20.289 --> 00:01:27.142
Every morning, a taxi came to pick up Mr. Darling in the dog house and took him to his office.

15
00:01:27.143 --> 00:01:30.980
In the evening, he came home the same way.

16
00:01:30.981 --> 00:01:34.434
Soon the news leaked out to his neighbors.

17
00:01:34.435 --> 00:01:40.134
They were saddened by the Darlings’ tragedy and by Mr. Darling’s grief.

18
00:01:40.135 --> 00:01:45.151
Crowds would follow his taxi home, touched by his devotion.

19
00:01:45.152 --> 00:01:51.543
On the day of the children’s return, Mrs. Darling was in the nursery waiting for her husband.

20
00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:54.230
She was a very sad woman now.

21
00:01:54.231 --> 00:01:58.975
She had lost her cheerfulness when she lost her children.

22
00:01:58.976 --> 00:02:05.003
The sparkle in the right corner of her mouth, where she kept her secret kiss, had dimmed.

23
00:02:05.004 --> 00:02:12.033
Tearfully she said to Nana, "Last night, I dreamed my little ones had come home."

24
00:02:12.034 --> 00:02:15.592
Nana put her paw gently on Mrs. Darling's lap.

25
00:02:15.593 --> 00:02:21.047
And there they sat until George was brought home in his dog house.

26
00:02:21.048 --> 00:02:26.382
When he arrived home from work, Mr. Darling was carried up to the nursery.

27
00:02:26.383 --> 00:02:30.214
He stuck his head out of the dog house to kiss his wife.

28
00:02:30.215 --> 00:02:40.763
He sat like that for a while, with his head outside the dog house, talking to Mrs. Darling and holding her hand.

29
00:02:40.764 --> 00:02:46.874
"I am so full of sadness and regret," he sighed.

30
00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:50.119
Then he curled up in his dog house for a nap.

31
00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:55.415
"Won’t you play me something on the piano to put me to sleep?" he asked.

32
00:02:55.416 --> 00:03:00.576
"And shut the nursery window, dear. I feel a chilly draft."

33
00:03:00.577 --> 00:03:05.901
"Oh, George, don’t ever ask me to do that!" said Mrs. Darling.

34
00:03:05.902 --> 00:03:10.186
"The window must always be left open for the children."

35
00:03:10.187 --> 00:03:15.810
Mr. Darling apologized, and Mrs. Darling went into the other room to play the piano.

36
00:03:15.811 --> 00:03:18.270
Soon he was asleep.

37
00:03:18.271 --> 00:03:24.269
And while he slept, Peter and Tinker Bell flew into the nursery.

38
00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:29.284
After defeating the pirates, Peter could have returned to his underground home.

39
00:03:29.285 --> 00:03:37.933
He could have stayed there and let Tinker Bell guide Wendy, John, and Michael home—just as he had first planned.

40
00:03:37.934 --> 00:03:41.152
But Peter had changed his mind.

41
00:03:41.153 --> 00:03:46.272
He sailed on the Jolly Roger because he had come up with a new scheme.

42
00:03:46.273 --> 00:03:51.446
He and Tinker Bell arrived ahead of the others to put his scheme into action.

43
00:03:51.447 --> 00:03:55.706
"Quick, Tink," Peter whispered, "close the window!

44
00:03:55.707 --> 00:03:58.614
Now you and I must hide by the door.

45
00:03:58.615 --> 00:04:03.620
When Wendy flies by, she will think her mother has shut her out forever.

46
00:04:03.621 --> 00:04:10.574
Then she will have to go back to Neverland with me."

